WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.733 --> 00:00:03.200
Six-thirty in the morning.

2
00:00:03.633 --> 00:00:05.400
Lagos is already awake.

3
00:00:05.833 --> 00:00:07.100
And for millions of us,

4
00:00:07.433 --> 00:00:10.033
getting to work is the
hardest part of the day.

5
00:00:11.967 --> 00:00:13.267
You know this feeling.

6
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:14.367
It's late.

7
00:00:14.633 --> 00:00:16.800
You have been at the
bus stop for too long.

8
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.567
A bus finally stops, and the
conductor calls out your stop.

9
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.600
You enter, relieved.

10
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.067
The door closes.

11
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.800
And something does not feel right.

12
00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:28.700
Maybe it happened to you.

13
00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:30.133
Maybe to your sister.

14
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.167
Your colleague.

15
00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:32.100
Your friend.

16
00:00:32.733 --> 00:00:35.400
In Lagos, we call it one chance.

17
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.500
Police say these gangs pose as
passengers in commercial buses.

18
00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:41.300
And in a recent Lagos study,

19
00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:45.167
nearly nine in ten people said
they live in constant fear of it,

20
00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:47.033
mostly when they rush out early,

21
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.333
or rush home late.

22
00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:52.333
And it's not only about safety.

23
00:00:52.833 --> 00:00:55.533
When we asked people in
Lagos what they need most,

24
00:00:55.967 --> 00:00:57.800
nine in ten said price.

25
00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.367
For the same route, a ride-hailing
car can cost up to six times the

26
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.000
danfo fare.

27
00:01:03.733 --> 00:01:06.733
Eight in ten said safety
is extremely important.

28
00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.200
And more than half rated
the danfo two out of five,

29
00:01:10.233 --> 00:01:10.933
or less.

30
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.100
So every day, people choose
between a car they cannot afford,

31
00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:17.100
and a bus they do not trust.

32
00:01:17.633 --> 00:01:20.400
Meanwhile, vehicles
pass them every morning,

33
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.533
going their way, with empty seats.

34
00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.367
People have tried to fix this.

35
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:28.000
Ride-hailing sends a car just for you,

36
00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:30.600
so it costs too much to use every day.

37
00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:32.967
Carpool apps want you to book ahead,

38
00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:35.300
but in Lagos, plans change.

39
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:37.467
Shuttles run at fixed times.

40
00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.600
Miss one, and you are stranded.

41
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.800
Now meet Tunde.

42
00:01:42.233 --> 00:01:43.433
He works on the Island.

43
00:01:43.733 --> 00:01:46.933
His neighbour Emeka drives to
the Island every morning too.

44
00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.100
Same street.

45
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.100
Same time.

46
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:50.833
Three empty seats.

47
00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:55.400
With TagRides, Tunde sees
that Emeka is going his way.

48
00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:58.133
Tunde offers four
hundred and fifty naira.

49
00:01:58.533 --> 00:02:00.800
Emeka replies with
five hundred and fifty.

50
00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:05.233
Tunde accepts, and the fare is agreed
before he even leaves the house.

51
00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.100
And before Emeka arrives,

52
00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:08.933
Tunde already knows his name,

53
00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.133
his face, and his plate number.

54
00:02:11.933 --> 00:02:15.433
On the way, Funmi is waiting
at the bus stop in Adekunle.

55
00:02:15.933 --> 00:02:17.367
She is going the same way.

56
00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:18.900
Emeka stops.

57
00:02:19.233 --> 00:02:20.033
She enters.

58
00:02:20.533 --> 00:02:21.667
No going off route.

59
00:02:22.533 --> 00:02:25.467
This is why TagRides works
where others did not.

60
00:02:25.967 --> 00:02:28.067
TagRides only suggests a fare.

61
00:02:28.433 --> 00:02:30.667
The rider and the driver agree on it.

62
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.967
And because the driver
was going anyway,

63
00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:35.600
even a small fare is
extra money for him.

64
00:02:35.967 --> 00:02:38.367
So the price can come
close to the danfo fare,

65
00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.000
and sometimes even lower,

66
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.833
depending on the time and the driver.

67
00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:44.100
You know who you are entering with,

68
00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.000
and every trip has a record.

69
00:02:46.333 --> 00:02:48.300
The driver never leaves his road.

70
00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:52.433
And when we asked, seven in ten
said they want exactly this.

71
00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:55.633
And if you are the one driving,

72
00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:56.400
like Emeka?

73
00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.933
TagRides works with any vehicle.

74
00:02:59.233 --> 00:02:59.733
Car.

75
00:02:59.933 --> 00:03:00.633
Danfo.

76
00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:01.567
Staff bus.

77
00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:02.200
Keke.

78
00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.400
Okada, where it is allowed.

79
00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:07.267
And you control the seats
you're offering for the session.

80
00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:08.767
You were going anyway.

81
00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.467
Now your empty seats
help pay for your fuel.

82
00:03:12.533 --> 00:03:15.500
The more riders join, the
more money for drivers.

83
00:03:15.733 --> 00:03:18.767
The more drivers join, the
more options for riders.

84
00:03:19.233 --> 00:03:22.500
Twenty-two million trips
happen in Lagos every day.

85
00:03:22.833 --> 00:03:27.733
Across Africa, seven in ten city
trips are on foot or public transport.

86
00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.133
But we are not starting everywhere.

87
00:03:31.433 --> 00:03:32.967
We are starting with one road:

88
00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.167
Yaba to Lagos Island.

89
00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.400
We do it well.

90
00:03:36.967 --> 00:03:38.267
Then the next one.

91
00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:41.400
The car is going there anyway.

92
00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:42.533
TagRides.

93
00:03:42.867 --> 00:03:43.633
Their route.

94
00:03:43.933 --> 00:03:44.633
Your ride.
